                <pb facs="0563" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 15778/86A.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Squiers.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Adee refers to legation’s telegram of July 22 and instructs Mr. Squiers to
                    insist upon a settlement of the case of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Columbia</hi> in accordance with previous instructions, and says the
                    department is unable to submit <hi rendition="#italic">Buffalo</hi> case to a
                    mixed commission as proposed by Panama. Mr. Adee adds that the department’s
                    position has been set forth in repeated instructions.</p>
            </div>
